fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1006", description: some(value: "`anthill-todo list` orders ids LEXICOGRAPHICALLY, so at id 1000 the newest items stop appearing last.\n\nREPORTED BY USER, 2026-08-05, on the real project: \"list does not show\nWI-XXXX where XXXX > 1000\". They were shown — buried mid-list.\n\nMEASURED, before the fix, on the project's own data:\n  WI-093 WI-094 WI-1000 WI-1002 WI-1003 WI-1004 WI-1005 WI-102 WI-128 ...\n\"WI-1000\" compares below \"WI-102\" at the fourth character, so every\nfour-digit item wedges between WI-094 and WI-102.\n\nCAUSE. main.anthill's `merge_by_id` compared whole id STRINGS with\n`Ordered.lt`. Its caller `chrono_topo` documents the top-level cursor as\nadvancing CHRONOLOGICALLY, and ids are allocated monotonically (`max + 1`,\nanthill-todo/src/main.rs), so the number IS the age — which is what makes\nnumeric order the chronological one and the string compare simply wrong.\n\nFIX. `id_before` compares the trailing DIGIT RUN, leading zeros dropped, by\n(length, then code units) — numeric order once no leading zero survives, and\nneeding no string->Int64 parse, which `anthill.prelude.String` does not\ndeclare. Ties fall back to the whole id so the order stays TOTAL and the\nmerge sort stays stable and deterministic; an id with no digit run gives \"\"\nand sorts first, a defined place rather than a trap.\n\nTHE ZERO-STRIP IS LOAD-BEARING and has its own test, because the tempting\nsimplification (compare the digit run AS WRITTEN by length) gets the reported\ncase right and \"WI-0094\" vs \"WI-999\" backwards.\n\nTESTS: cmd_list_id_order_test (3). Both backouts were RUN, and the two\nfailing rows are not interchangeable — restoring `lt` fails only\nfour_digit_ids_sort_after_three_digit; dropping `drop_leading_zeros` fails\nonly zero_padding_does_not_decide_the_order. ids_below_the_boundary_are_\nunchanged passes in all three configurations, by design."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-05T02:35:57Z"))
